#: src/Plugin.php:179
msgid "The plugin sets no cookies and uses no browser storage, fingerprints, external spam service or external IP lookup. It stores digests of used random tokens for up to two hours; scheduled cleanup removes expired digests. Daily aggregate counts are kept for the configured period (30 days by default). The total rejected-comment count stays until the statistics are reset. Optional quarantine encrypts selected names, email addresses and message fields on this website, for seven days by default, up to 30 days and 500 records. Password, hidden, payment and file fields are excluded. Privacy-conscious mode prevents new quarantine capture, country filters, administrator summary emails and pingbacks/trackbacks; it does not delete existing records. If pingbacks are allowed, WordPress requests the source page and may send it the sender's IP address. Optional country filters use local GeoIP data or metadata from explicitly trusted infrastructure; Rocketsky Antispam does not store the IP address. Optional daily administrator emails contain counts only. Optional cleanup permanently deletes WordPress spam comments older than the configured age. Scheduled cleanup depends on WordPress cron and can run late. WordPress privacy tools export or erase quarantine records matching the contact email address. WordPress, form plugins, hosting, mail delivery and backups have their own data handling. Adapt this notice to your enabled settings, retention, infrastructure and legal basis."
msgstr ""

